  "instruction": "Consider the nations who joined the League of Nations on January 10th 1920, who were also part of the 51 original members of the United Nations. Of these nations, which one was the latest to join the Allies side in WWII?",
  "answer": "Based on my research:\n\n**League of Nations founding members (Jan 10, 1920) who were also original UN members (51 in 1945):**\nBelgium, Bolivia, Brazil, Canada, Australia, South Africa, New Zealand, India, UK, Cuba, France, Greece, Guatemala, Haiti, Liberia, Nicaragua, Panama, Peru, Poland, Yugoslavia, Czechoslovakia, Uruguay.\n\n**Dates they joined the Allies in WWII (declarations of war on Germany/Japan):**\n- Most joined 1939–1942 (UK, France, Canada, Australia, etc.)\n- **Peru**: February 12, 1945\n- **Uruguay**: February 15, 1945\n\n**Answer: Uruguay** — it declared war on Germany and Japan on February 15, 1945, the latest among this group.",
